  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from seven adult epilepsy patients undergoing extended clinical monitoring at Stanford Hospital, collected during brief aversive air puffs to the eye and during a 40-minute ketamine infusion (0.5 mg/kg). This BIDS-iEEG derivative represents the authors' NWB release (DANDI 001347), downsampled to 200 Hz, with 20-minute windows per recording and contact labels but no coordinates. The data support study of the brain-wide emergence of emotional responses to sensory experience and their modulation by a dissociative drug.",
  "methods_description": "sEEG was recorded with a Nihon Kohden JE-120 amplifier in patients with clinically placed depth electrodes. Signals were low-pass filtered with an FIR anti-aliasing filter and downsampled to 200 Hz, and 20-minute windows (10 min before and after the start of the eyepuff series) were exported to NWB. NWB files were converted to BrainVision float32 microvolts for BIDS-iEEG, with no further filtering or re-referencing.",
